Make relate_near's corner-distance test do what its comment says.

Upstream pin: VLA-3D @ a0c023c9662bd875f0b3aeff4ff60adc1991e449

relate_near first tests centre distance, then falls back to "object near if at least two points
close to each other" over the box corners. The fallback is written np.any(dists < thr) > 1:
np.any returns a bool, and a bool is never > 1, so the fallback never fires and near is centre
distance alone -- two long objects touching end to end are never near. This counts the close
corner pairs instead, as the comment describes.

Without it: near silently ignores box extent, which matters for us because our boxes are
anisotropic (thin in depth; see reifyscene/graph/relations.py).

